invariant: INV-14
file: srv_resume.c
catches: srv_flight_test
reason: a server with no clock issues and accepts tickets. With now_seconds 0 it
  writes 0 as every ticket's instant, and a later server with a clock
  judges those tickets as issued at its epoch, which is decades stale or,
  on a clock that counts from boot, fresh for a week after every boot.
  srv_cfg.h makes a missing clock mean no tickets. test/srv_resume_tests.h
  clears the clock and requires that nothing is sent.

--- old
    return srv->ticket_key != NULL && srv->now_seconds != 0;
--- new
    return srv->ticket_key != NULL;
